
**Required output format (structural audit — MANDATORY):**

End with exactly one fenced JSON object and emit no textual decision line.
Implementation authority is represented only by the live GitHub
implementation-state label after the PR exists; this pre-PR compatibility
review remains informational.

```json
{"verdict": "GO", "grade": "A", "summary": "...", "comments": [
  {"path": "...", "line": 1, "side": "RIGHT", "severity": "major", "body": "..."}
], "scope_expansions": []}
```

`verdict` is one of `GO`, `NOGO`, or `BLOCKED`. The field is required. `GO`
states that the code meets the review criteria. A missing or malformed verdict
is invalid. `grade` is informational and is one of `A`, `B`, `C`, `D`, `E`,
or `F`; `summary` is a concise informational summary; `comments` is an array
of concrete findings; and
`scope_expansions` is an array of child-issue prerequisites that must not be
routed to the current branch. Each comment must provide a repository-relative
`path`, positive changed-line `line`, `"RIGHT"` side, one of `critical`,
`major`, `minor`, or `nitpick` severity, and actionable `body`. Emit an empty
`comments` array only when no findings remain. Emit an empty
`scope_expansions` array when there is no required child issue. Do not emit
`Verdict:` or any other textual decision line.
